Name: voiceCommand

Type: message

Syntax: voiceCommand <phrase>

Summary:
Sent to the current card of the default stack when the speech recognition
engine recognises a registered voice command phrase.

Introduced: 1.0.0

OS: mac, Windows, Linux

Platforms: desktop

Example:
-- Handle recognised commands in a card script
on voiceCommand pPhrase
    switch pPhrase
        case "next slide"
            go next card
            break
        case "previous slide"
            go prev card
            break
        case "save stack"
            save this stack
            break
    end switch
end voiceCommand

Example:
-- Forward the command to a handler named after the phrase
on voiceCommand pPhrase
    -- Strip spaces and capitalise for a handler name, e.g. "open stack" → "doOpenStack"
    put word 1 to -1 of pPhrase into tWords
    put "do" before tWords
    send tWords to this card
end voiceCommand

Parameters:
phrase (string): The registered phrase that was recognised. The value
matches one of the strings previously passed to <registerVoiceCommand>,
preserving the original capitalisation used at registration time.

Description:
The engine dispatches <voiceCommand> whenever a spoken utterance matches
a phrase registered with <registerVoiceCommand> and the engine is active
(see <startListening>).

When a wake word is set (see <setWakeWord>), <voiceCommand> is only
dispatched during the command window that opens after the wake word is
detected — it is not fired for the wake word itself.

The message is sent to the current card of the stack that registered
the matched phrase (captured at the time <registerVoiceCommand> was
called). It then bubbles up the normal HyperXTalk message path.

The first matched phrase wins; if multiple registered phrases could
match a single utterance, only the first match (in registration order)
fires.

References: registerVoiceCommand (command), startListening (command),
setWakeWord (command), wakeWordDetected (message), isListening (function)

Tags: speech, voice
